# track=guilds — relational Guilds schema. Versions match schema_migrations.
1 initial Initial database schema creation
2 spawn Add spawn location columns to guilds table
3 home-block-y Add home_block_y column to guilds table for better spawn fallback
4 level-system Add guild level system with resource contributions and tech tree points
5 bitwise-permissions Convert GuildBlock permissions to bitwise system using GuildPermission flag values
6 toggles Add guild toggle system with dedicated boolean columns
7 plot-types Add extensible plot type system with registry support
8 broadcasts Add guild broadcasting system with message types, priorities, and audience targeting
9 tech-tree Add tech tree system with node definitions and guild unlock tracking
10 economy Add economy transactions table for economy audit log
11 nations Add nation system tables for nation mechanics
12 specializations Add guild specialization system with specialization tracking
13 quests Add guild quests system with quest tracking and rewards
14 blueprints Add blueprints table for building templates and schematics
15 governance-form Add governance form columns to guilds and nations
16 rename-towns Rename legacy town schema objects to guild naming
17 retire-blueprints Retire blueprint feature (table preserved for operator cleanup)
18 rename-nations Rename nation schema objects to alliance naming
19 contracts Add guild contracts table for cross-guild level-up material contracts
20 last-online Widen residents.last_online from INTEGER to BIGINT to match the long-typed model
21 bank-enrollment Add guild bank player enrollment tracking
22 projects Add active guild project slot and default project skill points
23 projects-tech-points Backfill tech_points column on legacy installs skipped by v4
24 guild-storage Add guild storage item bank tables
25 guild-storage-operations Add durable guild storage mutation operation journal
26 guild-storage-audit-operation Add operation identity to guild storage audit records
